{
 "about": "Marks on printed parts' edges, in pixels of 1280x720 frames of the Prusa CORE One's camera as it stood on 2026-09-27 and 2026-10-08, from the recordings' own frames: fan-cut-bridge, under-extrusion-lace and spaghetti-small-nest (27 September) and petg-spool-jam-air-print (8 October). That camera streamed 1280x720 then, so no 1920x1080 calibration fits these frames. Its chassis landmarks match within a pixel across both dates, so one calibration serves both. Each curve's points lie on the planned outline `what` names at height `z` (`top`: that layer's outer walls; `first`: the first layer's extrusions, here the parts' edges against the sheet). `zc_mm` is the height the print had reached when the frame was taken, read off the slice at the frame's recorded progress; the two `05-finished` frames were taken with the bed parked at Z 31, the slice's own last move (max layer 30 + 1). The 27 September points were read by hand off part corners and edges on zoomed crops. The 8 October points, on two frames before its extrusion stopped at about Z 2, were each placed on the strongest brightness edge within 3 px of the 27 September fit's projection of the part's walls, keeping only points on parts away from the purge bin, whose wall reads ambiguously against its dark band, and only points whose nearest wall segment the tool's fit can match. The landmarks are core-one-2026-10-09.json's, found in these frames at two thirds of their 1920x1080 positions. The calibration beside this file is the tool's fit of these marks, started from its fit of the 27 September frames' marks alone, which it fits from its own generic starts.",
